## **4. Document permission matrix**

Permissions must be assigned by role, document category, ownership, department, campus and workflow state.

| Role            | Create           | View                            | Edit             | Approve               | Issue    |
| --------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------- | -------- |
| Super Admin     | Config only      | Technical metadata              | Templates/config | No automatic approval | No       |
| Administrator   | Yes              | Authorized                      | Authorized       | Assigned              | Assigned |
| Principal       | Yes              | Authorized                      | Own/assigned     | Assigned              | Assigned |
| Registrar       | Yes              | Academic                        | Academic         | Academic              | Academic |
| Finance Officer | Yes              | Finance                         | Finance          | Assigned finance      | Finance  |
| HR Officer      | Yes              | HR                              | HR               | Assigned HR           | HR       |
| Lecturer        | Yes              | Assigned academic               | Own/assigned     | Assigned              | No       |
| HOD             | Yes              | Department                      | Department       | Department            | Assigned |
| Librarian       | Yes              | Library                         | Library          | Assigned              | Library  |
| Student         | Personal uploads | Own permitted files             | Drafts/own files | No                    | No       |
| Parent          | No               | Authorized linked student files | No               | No                    | No       |

**Critical security rule:** a Super Admin must not automatically gain access to confidential counselling records, HR files, student financial details or private academic documents merely because they administer the platform.

